1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,769
In lesson one, you used CloudCart. In lesson two, you built it. Today, you deploy it.

2
00:00:06,319 --> 00:00:11,802
Deploy means one thing: put the war file where Tomcat can find it, and let Tomcat run it.

3
00:00:12,352 --> 00:00:13,918
You will do it two ways.

4
00:00:13,918 --> 00:00:14,439
By hand,

5
00:00:14,439 --> 00:00:15,875
with one copy command.

6
00:00:15,875 --> 00:00:17,245
And from the Manager,

7
00:00:17,245 --> 00:00:20,245
the web page Tomcat gives every administrator.

8
00:00:20,795 --> 00:00:21,513
By the end,

9
00:00:21,513 --> 00:00:24,120
one Tomcat runs two copies of CloudCart.

10
00:00:24,120 --> 00:00:25,881
And you remove one of them,

11
00:00:25,881 --> 00:00:26,598
on purpose.

12
00:00:28,148 --> 00:00:31,220
Here is what to expect, from the first minute to the last.

13
00:00:31,770 --> 00:00:36,442
One: see an empty Tomcat. It runs, but it has no CloudCart inside.

14
00:00:36,992 --> 00:00:42,048
Two: deploy by hand. Copy one file, and watch Tomcat unpack it and start it.

15
00:00:42,598 --> 00:00:47,078
Three: the Manager. A web page where you deploy, and remove, with the mouse.

16
00:00:47,628 --> 00:00:51,084
Four: your turn. A lab, where one check judges all of it.

17
00:00:51,634 --> 00:00:56,083
And two lessons ahead: run it like a customer and fix it like an engineer,

18
00:00:56,083 --> 00:00:58,247
then prove it all from a clean copy.

19
00:00:58,797 --> 00:01:00,760
See it, copy it, click it, prove it.

20
00:01:02,810 --> 00:01:06,223
Before we deploy, one picture: how Tomcat finds an app.

21
00:01:06,773 --> 00:01:09,931
Tomcat watches one folder. It is called webapps.

22
00:01:10,481 --> 00:01:12,028
Drop a war file in it.

23
00:01:12,028 --> 00:01:14,421
The file name becomes the address.

24
00:01:14,421 --> 00:01:17,094
cloudcart.war becomes /cloudcart.

25
00:01:17,644 --> 00:01:22,743
Tomcat unpacks the war into a folder with the same name, and starts the app inside it.

26
00:01:23,293 --> 00:01:27,197
Remove the war, and Tomcat stops the app, and deletes that folder.

27
00:01:27,747 --> 00:01:28,421
File name,

28
00:01:28,421 --> 00:01:28,961
address,

29
00:01:28,961 --> 00:01:29,434
unpack,

30
00:01:29,434 --> 00:01:29,838
start.

31
00:01:29,838 --> 00:01:31,053
Keep this picture.

32
00:01:31,053 --> 00:01:33,077
The Manager does the same job,

33
00:01:33,077 --> 00:01:33,955
with buttons.

34
00:01:35,505 --> 00:01:40,497
Go to the lab folder.

35
00:01:42,047 --> 00:01:43,946
Look around. Type: L S.

36
00:01:44,496 --> 00:01:45,202
Two files,

37
00:01:45,202 --> 00:01:46,121
and a folder.

38
00:01:46,121 --> 00:01:48,312
Tomcat is in the tomcat folder.

39
00:01:48,312 --> 00:01:49,160
And the app,

40
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:50,644
packed in a war file,

41
00:01:50,644 --> 00:01:52,623
twice: once named cloudcart,

42
00:01:52,623 --> 00:01:54,037
and once named shop.

43
00:01:54,037 --> 00:01:54,956
The same app,

44
00:01:54,956 --> 00:01:56,016
with two names.

45
00:01:56,566 --> 00:02:01,280
Look inside webapps.

46
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:07,718
One folder only: manager. That is Tomcat's own admin app. CloudCart is not here.

47
00:02:08,268 --> 00:02:13,623
Start Tomcat, and keep the last line.

48
00:02:14,173 --> 00:02:18,290
Tomcat started. It is running, but it has no CloudCart to serve.

49
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:28,910
Ask for CloudCart, and keep the first line.

50
00:02:29,460 --> 00:02:30,295
Four oh four.

51
00:02:30,295 --> 00:02:30,937
Not found.

52
00:02:30,937 --> 00:02:32,157
The server is fine.

53
00:02:32,157 --> 00:02:33,506
The app is not there.

54
00:02:33,506 --> 00:02:34,726
Now the same thing,

55
00:02:34,726 --> 00:02:35,689
in the browser.

56
00:02:36,239 --> 00:02:41,722
Open Chrome, and go to localhost:8089/cloudcart.

57
00:02:46,972 --> 00:02:48,104
The same answer,

58
00:02:48,104 --> 00:02:50,865
as a page: HTTP status four oh four.

59
00:02:50,865 --> 00:02:51,785
Tomcat is on,

60
00:02:51,785 --> 00:02:54,758
and says: I found nothing at this address.

61
00:02:55,308 --> 00:03:00,962
Now the Manager. Go to /manager/html. The browser asks who you are.

62
00:03:05,012 --> 00:03:10,091
Tomcat never lets anyone into the Manager without a name and a password.

63
00:03:10,091 --> 00:03:10,866
In the lab,

64
00:03:10,866 --> 00:03:12,136
they are deployer,

65
00:03:12,136 --> 00:03:14,605
and ship-it-115.

66
00:03:14,605 --> 00:03:16,721
They live in one file: tomcat,

67
00:03:16,721 --> 00:03:17,074
conf,

68
00:03:17,074 --> 00:03:19,049
tomcat-users.xml.

69
00:03:19,599 --> 00:03:22,557
This is the Tomcat Web Application Manager.

70
00:03:22,557 --> 00:03:23,314
At the top,

71
00:03:23,314 --> 00:03:24,483
the message line.

72
00:03:24,483 --> 00:03:25,309
It says OK,

73
00:03:25,309 --> 00:03:27,304
or tells you what went wrong.

74
00:03:27,304 --> 00:03:29,092
Read it after every click.

75
00:03:29,642 --> 00:03:29,978
Next,

76
00:03:29,978 --> 00:03:30,649
the links.

77
00:03:30,649 --> 00:03:31,856
List applications,

78
00:03:31,856 --> 00:03:32,862
two help pages,

79
00:03:32,862 --> 00:03:34,070
and server status,

80
00:03:34,070 --> 00:03:36,149
which shows memory and threads.

81
00:03:36,699 --> 00:03:40,221
Then the heart of the page: the Applications table.

82
00:03:40,221 --> 00:03:42,500
One row for each app Tomcat runs.

83
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:42,915
Today,

84
00:03:42,915 --> 00:03:44,572
only the manager itself.

85
00:03:44,572 --> 00:03:46,092
The columns: the path,

86
00:03:46,092 --> 00:03:47,542
which is the address.

87
00:03:47,542 --> 00:03:48,371
The version.

88
00:03:48,371 --> 00:03:49,545
The display name.

89
00:03:49,545 --> 00:03:50,097
Running,

90
00:03:50,097 --> 00:03:51,064
true or false.

91
00:03:51,064 --> 00:03:51,686
Sessions,

92
00:03:51,686 --> 00:03:53,274
the visitors right now.

93
00:03:53,274 --> 00:03:54,448
And the commands.

94
00:03:54,998 --> 00:03:55,916
Four commands.

95
00:03:55,916 --> 00:03:57,556
Start brings an app back.

96
00:03:57,556 --> 00:03:58,933
Stop switches it off,

97
00:03:58,933 --> 00:04:00,441
but keeps it installed.

98
00:04:00,441 --> 00:04:02,343
Reload restarts it from disk.

99
00:04:02,343 --> 00:04:03,654
Undeploy removes it.

100
00:04:03,654 --> 00:04:09,228
For the manager itself they are plain text: you cannot remove the tool you are using.

101
00:04:09,778 --> 00:04:10,170
Below,

102
00:04:10,170 --> 00:04:11,412
the Deploy section.

103
00:04:11,412 --> 00:04:13,635
The first form deploys a war file,

104
00:04:13,635 --> 00:04:14,419
or a folder,

105
00:04:14,419 --> 00:04:16,380
that is already on the server.

106
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:17,361
A context path,

107
00:04:17,361 --> 00:04:19,322
which is the address you want.

108
00:04:19,322 --> 00:04:20,956
And the path of the file.

109
00:04:21,506 --> 00:04:24,564
The second form uploads a war from your own computer,

110
00:04:24,564 --> 00:04:25,545
with choose file.

111
00:04:25,545 --> 00:04:26,757
We use the first one,

112
00:04:26,757 --> 00:04:29,122
because our war is already on the server.

113
00:04:29,672 --> 00:04:32,597
Scroll down to the end: Server information.

114
00:04:32,597 --> 00:04:33,889
The Tomcat version,

115
00:04:33,889 --> 00:04:35,114
the JVM version,

116
00:04:35,114 --> 00:04:36,542
the operating system,

117
00:04:36,542 --> 00:04:37,426
and the host.

118
00:04:37,426 --> 00:04:38,650
When someone says,

119
00:04:38,650 --> 00:04:40,147
it works on my server,

120
00:04:40,147 --> 00:04:41,235
look here first.

121
00:04:41,785 --> 00:04:51,492
Method one, by hand. Copy the war into webapps, and name it cloudcart.war.

122
00:04:52,042 --> 00:04:53,866
That is the whole deployment.

123
00:04:53,866 --> 00:04:56,697
Tomcat looks at the folder every few seconds.

124
00:04:56,697 --> 00:04:57,263
Wait ten,

125
00:04:57,263 --> 00:04:58,207
and look again.

126
00:04:58,757 --> 00:05:02,640
Wait, then list webapps.

127
00:05:03,190 --> 00:05:04,367
Three names now.

128
00:05:04,367 --> 00:05:04,956
manager,

129
00:05:04,956 --> 00:05:05,692
as before.

130
00:05:05,692 --> 00:05:06,722
cloudcart.war,

131
00:05:06,722 --> 00:05:08,120
the file we copied.

132
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:10,181
And a new folder: cloudcart.

133
00:05:10,181 --> 00:05:11,947
Tomcat unpacked the war,

134
00:05:11,947 --> 00:05:14,155
and started the app inside it.

135
00:05:14,705 --> 00:05:16,787
Back to the browser.

136
00:05:16,787 --> 00:05:19,182
Open the Manager again,

137
00:05:19,182 --> 00:05:24,284
at the same address: localhost:8089/manager/html.

138
00:05:24,834 --> 00:05:26,730
A new row: /cloudcart.

139
00:05:26,730 --> 00:05:27,714
Running: true.

140
00:05:27,714 --> 00:05:28,557
No sessions,

141
00:05:28,557 --> 00:05:30,735
because nobody has visited yet.

142
00:05:30,735 --> 00:05:32,983
Tomcat found the app on its own.

143
00:05:33,533 --> 00:05:34,563
Click the path,

144
00:05:34,563 --> 00:05:35,799
and the app opens.

145
00:05:35,799 --> 00:05:37,584
Scroll down to the footer.

146
00:05:37,584 --> 00:05:41,154
Version zero point two point oh: the same CloudCart,

147
00:05:41,154 --> 00:05:42,321
deployed by hand,

148
00:05:42,321 --> 00:05:43,282
with one copy.

149
00:05:43,832 --> 00:05:49,230
Method two, the Manager. Open the same address again, and look at the table: two rows now.

150
00:05:53,580 --> 00:05:58,422
In the deploy form, the context path is the address you want. Type: /shop.

151
00:05:58,972 --> 00:06:02,101
And the path of the war on the server: file,

152
00:06:02,101 --> 00:06:02,528
colon,

153
00:06:02,528 --> 00:06:03,239
/opt,

154
00:06:03,239 --> 00:06:04,803
/lab115,

155
00:06:04,803 --> 00:06:06,155
/shop.war.

156
00:06:06,155 --> 00:06:07,079
Click deploy.

157
00:06:07,629 --> 00:06:09,144
The message says: OK,

158
00:06:09,144 --> 00:06:12,451
deployed application at context path /shop.

159
00:06:12,451 --> 00:06:14,173
And a third row appeared.

160
00:06:14,173 --> 00:06:14,930
One Tomcat,

161
00:06:14,930 --> 00:06:16,790
two copies of the same app,

162
00:06:16,790 --> 00:06:18,168
under two addresses.

163
00:06:18,718 --> 00:06:19,831
Click /shop.

164
00:06:19,831 --> 00:06:21,206
The same store opens.

165
00:06:21,206 --> 00:06:23,759
Scroll to the footer: the same version.

166
00:06:23,759 --> 00:06:26,116
Look at the address bar: /shop.

167
00:06:26,116 --> 00:06:26,771
This time,

168
00:06:26,771 --> 00:06:28,211
you chose the address.

169
00:06:28,761 --> 00:06:30,567
Now remove the first copy.

170
00:06:30,567 --> 00:06:32,165
Open the Manager again,

171
00:06:32,165 --> 00:06:33,554
at the same address.

172
00:06:33,554 --> 00:06:35,569
Find the /cloudcart row,

173
00:06:35,569 --> 00:06:36,889
and click undeploy.

174
00:06:38,739 --> 00:06:39,025
OK,

175
00:06:39,025 --> 00:06:42,033
undeployed application at /cloudcart.

176
00:06:42,033 --> 00:06:43,178
The row is gone.

177
00:06:43,178 --> 00:06:44,396
Only the manager,

178
00:06:44,396 --> 00:06:45,327
and the shop,

179
00:06:45,327 --> 00:06:45,971
are left.

180
00:06:46,521 --> 00:06:49,624
Open /cloudcart again: type the address,

181
00:06:49,624 --> 00:06:50,727
and press enter.

182
00:06:50,727 --> 00:06:51,623
Four oh four.

183
00:06:51,623 --> 00:06:51,968
Gone,

184
00:06:51,968 --> 00:06:53,829
as if it had never existed.

185
00:06:53,829 --> 00:06:56,036
And /shop is still running.

186
00:06:56,586 --> 00:07:01,514
Look at the disk.

187
00:07:02,064 --> 00:07:03,306
The cloudcart war,

188
00:07:03,306 --> 00:07:04,342
and its folder,

189
00:07:04,342 --> 00:07:04,963
are gone.

190
00:07:04,963 --> 00:07:07,379
And the Manager left shop.war here,

191
00:07:07,379 --> 00:07:08,483
with its folder,

192
00:07:08,483 --> 00:07:10,554
exactly like the copy by hand.

193
00:07:11,104 --> 00:07:17,910
Stop Tomcat, and keep the last line.

194
00:07:19,460 --> 00:07:20,228
Stopped.

195
00:07:20,778 --> 00:07:25,855
Is the port free? Count the lines.

196
00:07:26,405 --> 00:07:32,186
Zero. Nothing listens. Two ways to deploy, and one way to remove. All on a real server.

197
00:07:33,736 --> 00:07:37,555
Your task. Deploy CloudCart two ways, remove one, and prove it.

198
00:07:38,105 --> 00:07:42,883
One: lab up. Then start Tomcat. It starts with no CloudCart inside.

199
00:07:43,433 --> 00:07:44,361
Two: by hand.

200
00:07:44,361 --> 00:07:47,429
Copy the war into webapps as cloudcart.war,

201
00:07:47,429 --> 00:07:47,786
wait,

202
00:07:47,786 --> 00:07:48,999
and open the app.

203
00:07:48,999 --> 00:07:50,355
Then run lab check,

204
00:07:50,355 --> 00:07:51,711
so that it sees it.

205
00:07:52,261 --> 00:07:56,442
Three: in the Manager, deploy shop.war with the path /shop.

206
00:07:56,992 --> 00:08:00,107
Four: in the Manager, undeploy /cloudcart.

207
00:08:00,657 --> 00:08:02,269
Five: write answers.txt,

208
00:08:02,269 --> 00:08:03,075
three lines.

209
00:08:03,075 --> 00:08:04,888
The apps the Manager lists,

210
00:08:04,888 --> 00:08:07,441
and two answers about folders on disk.

211
00:08:07,991 --> 00:08:11,084
Six: lab check, five checks, and then lab down.

212
00:08:13,134 --> 00:08:17,337
Here is where to find everything. Pause on this screen if you need to write it down.

213
00:08:17,887 --> 00:08:19,535
The lab lives on GitHub,

214
00:08:19,535 --> 00:08:20,702
at it-waves,

215
00:08:20,702 --> 00:08:22,281
/devops-ai,

216
00:08:22,281 --> 00:08:23,792
in the folder academy,

217
00:08:23,792 --> 00:08:24,479
/lab.

218
00:08:25,029 --> 00:08:30,447
Two files: lab115.sh, and shortcuts115.sh.

219
00:08:30,997 --> 00:08:31,913
Install it,

220
00:08:31,913 --> 00:08:34,826
on any Linux machine: sudo install,

221
00:08:34,826 --> 00:08:36,740
-m 755,

222
00:08:36,740 --> 00:08:38,738
lab115.sh,

223
00:08:38,738 --> 00:08:39,986
into /usr,

224
00:08:39,986 --> 00:08:40,985
/local,

225
00:08:40,985 --> 00:08:41,984
/sbin.

226
00:08:42,534 --> 00:08:47,633
Load the short name with: source shortcuts115.sh. You get: lab.

227
00:08:48,183 --> 00:08:49,312
You need a JDK,

228
00:08:49,312 --> 00:08:49,644
curl,

229
00:08:49,644 --> 00:08:50,773
and the ss tool,

230
00:08:50,773 --> 00:08:52,698
about one gigabyte of memory,

231
00:08:52,698 --> 00:08:57,546
and ports eight thousand eighty-nine and eight thousand ninety-nine free.

232
00:08:57,546 --> 00:08:59,206
The lab downloads Tomcat,

233
00:08:59,206 --> 00:09:00,003
and the app,

234
00:09:00,003 --> 00:09:00,535
for you.

235
00:09:01,085 --> 00:09:07,250
The Manager login is deployer, and ship-it-115. It is a lab value only.

236
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:09,567
Lab check judges your work.

237
00:09:09,567 --> 00:09:12,511
Lab down stops Tomcat and removes everything.

238
00:09:12,511 --> 00:09:14,605
Only run it on your own machine.

239
00:09:16,655 --> 00:09:18,724
Pass or fail. You need all five.

240
00:09:19,274 --> 00:09:21,856
Tomcat runs, and the Manager answers.

241
00:09:22,406 --> 00:09:25,350
CloudCart was deployed by hand, and answered up.

242
00:09:25,900 --> 00:09:28,524
Slash shop runs, and the Manager lists it.

243
00:09:29,074 --> 00:09:32,551
Slash cloudcart is undeployed: gone, while shop stays.

244
00:09:33,101 --> 00:09:35,768
The three lines in answers.txt are right.

245
00:09:36,318 --> 00:09:37,619
To pass, all five.

246
00:09:39,669 --> 00:09:41,440
Your turn, on your own machine.

247
00:09:41,990 --> 00:09:45,019
One: lab up, read the task list, and start Tomcat.

248
00:09:45,569 --> 00:09:48,449
Two: copy the war in by hand, and open the app.

249
00:09:48,999 --> 00:09:51,751
Three: deploy shop.war from the Manager.

250
00:09:52,301 --> 00:09:54,456
Four: undeploy /cloudcart.

251
00:09:55,006 --> 00:09:59,656
Five: write the three answers, and run lab check, until you see five out of five.

252
00:10:00,206 --> 00:10:02,788
Six: lab down, and prove the port is free.

253
00:10:03,338 --> 00:10:05,172
Pause the video, and begin now.

254
00:10:20,722 --> 00:10:21,597
Quick check.

255
00:10:22,147 --> 00:10:24,557
Which folder does Tomcat watch for new apps?

256
00:10:25,107 --> 00:10:28,094
What decides the address of an app you drop in by hand?

257
00:10:28,644 --> 00:10:31,929
Which button removes an app, and which one only switches it off?

258
00:10:32,479 --> 00:10:35,210
What did the Manager do with shop.war on disk?

259
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:38,665
Objective covered: CloudCart version zero,

260
00:10:38,665 --> 00:10:40,048
deploy it to Tomcat,

261
00:10:40,048 --> 00:10:42,053
by hand and from the Manager.

262
00:10:42,603 --> 00:10:44,673
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

263
00:10:55,223 --> 00:10:58,721
Next: run it like a customer, and fix it like an engineer.

264
00:10:59,271 --> 00:11:02,599
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
